# File: tests/bdd/features/scaffold-plugin-repo-session-start-hooks.feature
# Generated from: specs/226-restore-the-two-second-return-bound-in-the-launcher-detach-scenarios/requirements.md
Feature: Launcher detach requires a return in under two seconds with the child still running

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A launcher passes only when it returns in under two seconds with its child alive
    Given a fake Blender and a fake UE editor that record their PID and keep running until stopped
    When scripts/start-blender-mcp.sh and scripts/start-unreal-mcp.sh each run against their fake
    Then each script exits 0 while the fake child it started is still alive
    And each script returns control to the shell in under two seconds

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A slow launcher fails the detach check
    Given a synthetic launcher that sleeps 2.5 seconds before detaching the fake child
    When it runs with a fake child that keeps running
    Then the detach check fails because the launcher took longer than two seconds
    And the launcher finished its 2.5 second delay before detaching

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: A launcher that waits for its child still fails the detach check
    Given a synthetic launcher that starts the fake child and waits for it
    When it runs with a child that exits after 1 second, and again with a child that keeps running under a 3 second bound
    Then the detach check fails the first run because the child is gone
    And the detach check fails the second run because the launcher did not return
